          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-93009"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "A flaw was found in dnsmasq. The DHCPv6 client hostname parser can read one byte past the end of a crafted FQDN option because it checks the next label length before confirming the pointer is still inside the option. An attacker on the local network can trigger this with a single DHCPv6 packet. The extra byte is not returned to the client or logged, and no crash has been demonstrated.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
